    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1213">

                <pb facs="1422" n="1224" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Potsdam/8–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1213<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State and the Ambassador to the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1213-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-19">19 July 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>ComNavGroup China sends. Top secret and urgent for the eyes alone of the
                    Secretary of State, James F. Byrnes, Potsdam, Germany.</p>
                <pb facs="1423" n="1225" xml:id="pg1225"/>
                <p>For Ambassador Harriman from Hurley (the following message is from Dr. T. V.
                    Soong for Ambassador Harriman).</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“After having had the opportunity of discussing the details of the
                            negotiations<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1213-f2"/> with Generalissimo<anchor
                            n="3" xml:id="d1213-f3"/> and other leading members of my Government, I
                        am convinced that we have gone as far as we possibly could in meeting Soviet
                        demands. I tell you this in all candor, and you know how completely frank I
                        have been with you. T. V. Soong”.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1213-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1213-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the Commander, Naval Group, China, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1213-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1213-f2-content">
                <p>i. e., Soong’s negotiations with Stalin at Moscow, which had been interrupted by
                    Stalin’s departure for the Berlin Conference. See <ref
                        target="frus1945Berlinv01#pg_857">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">i</hi>,
                        p. 857</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1213-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1213-f3-content">
                <p>Chiang Kai-shek.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
